e only after a read-only check of those 5 rows passes.\n\n**Why the earlier runs failed:** cycle 85 hit LabVIEW error 2 (memory full). The failure came from the whole-diagram read after every edit piling up memory, not from the edit at step 45.\n- Reads added 140 MB over a full replay, while the edits themselves added 1.7 MB.\n- With 9 reads instead of 43, all 42 edits landed and error 2 did not occur.\n- Whether the reads themselves or the total memory is the real cause is still open. The prior-art review stopped me from claiming it was the reads.\n\nThe stage now reads the whole diagram only at 9 checkpoints, and it stops at 700 MB. Every edit still checks its own connection.\n\n**Reviews:**\n- **Outcome review:** repeated the same four verdicts. The steering card said the next act must be a real build or run, and this cycle followed it by running the stage.\n- **Retrospective:** found no violation. Its one lesson is that one test this cycle ran on a prediction the simulation files already contradicted; next cycle checks predictions against those files first.\n\n**Next cycle's first act:** the read-only check of the 5 rows on the new file, with each prediction checked against the simulation files before LabVIEW is touched. If it passes, the file becomes the next base, and the next session chooses between:\n- L2 stage 2.\n- The outcome review's suggestion: swap the tracking call in the S1 copy to the verified parallel kernel, then measure lost frames at 15 beads.\n\n**Housekeeping:**\n- STATUS said 4 of your questions were still open. `decisions_pending.json` shows all 7 answered, so I marked that line stale. Nothing is waiting on you.\n- I added a small helper, `tools/waitlogs.py`, to wait on review logs without shell loops.\n- The Figma connector needs authorising in your claude.ai connector settings. Until then it can't be used.","ttft_ms":3112,"type":"result","duration_ms":6120064,"uuid":"de2630c9-63d4-4422-a55e-6ad04bfcebfa","ttft_stream_ms":3007,"time_to_requ